# When you need more networks, you need more bits 
  1- Network Address/ Subnet Address
      -The First Address in the subnet 
  2- Broadcast Address
      -The last Address in the subnet 
  3- First available Host address
      -One more than the network address 
  4- Last available Host address 
      -One less than the broadcast address 


 Classes 

/1 - /7   (Rare/Large Networks)

/8         (Class A) 

/9-/15      Subnetted Class A 

/ 16        (Class B)           

/17-/23     Subnetted Class B 

/24          Class C 

/25-/30      Subnetted Class C 

/31-/32      Special Use 


